# Tests for the dynamic-module-argument warning (G0129): a state
# instance's Port argument whose expression cone contains a source
# that is proven to vary within a clock cycle (wire reads, rule fire
# signals, ActionValue results) is wired combinationally in the
# generated Verilog with no scheduling relationship to its writers,
# so the submodule can observe it outside the atomic rule semantics.
# Register/constant-fed arguments (including through pure operators)
# stay silent.

compile_verilog_pass_warning DynArgWire.bsv G0129

compile_verilog_pass_no_warning DynArgReg.bsv
